From 8ce744a69b8c7ad056b4c5a9bc60525de339c0a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:29:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: VU1 program capture (PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE)

When PS2X_VU1_CAPTURE=<dir>[,N[,K]] names a directory, the VIF1 MSCAL and MSCNT callbacks hand every VU1 run to a Recorder (runtime/ps2_vu1_capture.h, read when syncCoreSubsystems binds the callbacks). A run is written as <dir>/vu1-<index>-<pc>.cap when fewer than N files exist (default 200), its key (kind, start pc, hash of the 16 KB micro memory) has fewer than K files (default 4), and no run with identical inputs (key, data memory, VU1 state without the cycle counter, TOP/ITOP/FBRST) was written. File: a 104-byte header (magic OBVU1CAP, version 1, kind, flags with budget hit, run index, start pc, TOP, ITOP, FBRST, VPU_STAT before/after, cycle budget, interpreter cycles run, code generation, code hash, input hash, section sizes, packet count), micro memory, data memory before, a fixed-layout VU1 state record before, data memory after, state after, then every PATH1 (XGKICK) packet the run sent as u32 size + bytes. The packets come from a PATH1 tap that VU1Interpreter::finishXgkick calls before submitting; offline tools use the same tap. <dir>/summary.txt (every 4096 runs and at each file) lists totals and per key the runs and interpreter cycles. Unset: the callbacks cost one null check and the tap one atomic load per XGKICK.
---
